# Family A2: fan-out storage architecture (internal/engine). See hack/bakeoff.sh.
PKG=./internal/engine
BENCH=BenchmarkMemory/FanOut
REF=persubenvelopes
AUTO_KEY=arch
KIND_DIM=arch
KINDS_TEST=TestArchKindsList
AUTO_FILE=./internal/engine/auto_arch.go
AUTO_PREFIX=Arch
ADR=14
TITLE="Fan-out storage architecture (A2)"
# The engine hosts two families, so the architecture has its own list test and
# its own generated binding:
#   hack/bakeoff.sh A2
# and `bakeoff decide` writes the binding with -auto-prefix Arch into
# internal/engine/auto_arch.go. The §9 criterion is
# throughput at 16 subscriptions *and* slow-subscriber isolation, which is the
# slow=1 arm; IQMQ_BENCH_MATRIX=full adds 256 subscriptions.

#
# CRITERION is the benchmark configuration's decision column for this row, quoted.
# MATRIX is the IQMQ_BENCH_MATRIX grid the campaign measures the family at.
# DECIDED_AT names the benchmark-name segments the criterion is read at, and
# DECIDED_ON the metrics; `make bench-lint` lists the family's benchmarks at
# the declared grid and fails when a term or a metric is missing from the rows
# every kind has in common, which is the only data `bakeoff decide` reads.
CRITERION="throughput at 16 subs *and* slow-subscriber isolation -> per-sub envelopes expected"
# MATRIX=default because the default grid already produces what the criterion
# is read at: fan-out 1/4/16/64 is §10.4's own ladder and contains the 16-sub
# row the criterion names, and slow={0,1} is the slow-subscriber arm. `full`
# only adds a 256-subscription width that no criterion in §9.1 or §10.4 reads,
# for 32 more rows per run.
MATRIX=default
DECIDED_AT="16 64 slow=0 slow=1"
DECIDED_ON="msgs/s ns/op partial/op"
# One `go test -bench '^BenchmarkMemory/FanOut(/|$)'` run measures both this
# family and A7: the 112 rows carry arch= and policy= together, and the two
# families differ only in which dimension `bakeoff decide` splits on. The
# campaign as it stands measures them twice, which is 1.25 h of a shared host
# for one run's worth of data.
SHARES_ROOT="A7"
